1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,452
Imagine returning to a course assignment after an interruption.

2
00:00:04,452 --> 00:00:07,904
Your checklist still exists, but the context is gone.

3
00:00:07,904 --> 00:00:11,357
What were you reading? What should you do next?

4
00:00:11,357 --> 00:00:14,809
NextStep is a small workspace designed around that return.

5
00:00:14,809 --> 00:00:20,946
Our example student and notes are fictional; this is a working prototype, not a user-study result.

6
00:00:22,946 --> 00:00:26,611
I start with a short plan for a climate policy brief.

7
00:00:26,611 --> 00:00:30,610
Each line is a concrete action. Completing one step reveals the next.

8
00:00:30,610 --> 00:00:33,942
There is no score, public feed or streak to recover.

9
00:00:33,942 --> 00:00:40,274
The plan stays visible when I need an overview, and focus mode removes the surrounding workspace when I want

10
00:00:40,274 --> 00:00:41,940
to work on one action.

11
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:46,814
The timer is optional and never marks work complete.

12
00:00:46,814 --> 00:00:53,840
Now I need to leave. I save a small amount of context and one exact next action: open the second source and

13
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:56,076
copy its citation. Saving pauses the timer.

14
00:00:56,076 --> 00:01:02,144
This is a breadcrumb attached to the current planned step, rather than another task that might get lost in

15
00:01:02,144 --> 00:01:02,783
the list.

16
00:01:04,783 --> 00:01:10,309
After a real reload, the return card is still here, with the same context and action.

17
00:01:10,309 --> 00:01:14,454
Resume brings that note into focus mode beside the original planned step.

18
00:01:14,454 --> 00:01:17,908
The student decides when the planned step is actually complete.

19
00:01:17,908 --> 00:01:22,744
The application does not infer completion from a timer or from reading the breadcrumb.

20
00:01:24,744 --> 00:01:27,689
Higher contrast and larger text are available.

21
00:01:27,689 --> 00:01:33,160
Labeled native controls, keyboard shortcuts and visible focus support different ways of navigating.

22
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:37,368
Quick capture parks a thought without changing the active step.

23
00:01:37,368 --> 00:01:44,943
Work stays in this browser. I can download a JSON backup and restore it only after explicitly confirming

24
00:01:44,943 --> 00:01:51,255
replacement. Damaged imports are rejected before changing current work, and stale tabs cannot silently overwrite

25
00:01:51,255 --> 00:01:52,097
another tab.

26
00:01:54,097 --> 00:02:01,680
Twenty automated tests pass. We also verified the primary loop, a real backup download and restore, and keyboard

27
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:08,842
navigation in the browser. The semantic accessibility audit has a defined scope; it does not establish WCAG

28
00:02:08,842 --> 00:02:13,898
conformance. We have not measured productivity gains or run a user study.

29
00:02:13,898 --> 00:02:20,639
NextStep demonstrates a practical idea: make the next action explicit, preserve its context, and leave a

30
00:02:20,639 --> 00:02:21,903
clearer way back.
